From 04595848c4ee9274bee77f3dfb17b1c5118415e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:30:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_NX2_TC_RT_REUSE: reuse the host images of dropped render
 targets by shape

Ocarina creates ~8,000 render targets per 600 frames in the market because it moves them to a new
address almost every frame; with EDEN_NX2_TC_RT_EVICT the old ones are dropped after a few frames.
With this switch their host images (plain 2D, one level, one layer, one sample, uncompressed) go
into a small pool keyed by format and size (8 per shape, 1 GiB in all) when the sentenced image is
destroyed, and the next image of that shape takes one instead of creating and allocating a new
VkImage. The TC log reports reuses, misses and the pooled size.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HmEAGe4MCAJnHoeqq7Uysk
